    {
      "id": "claim_3366eb4f83264ce092199a4bb1295ccb",
      "statement": "infrastructure-as-code/ defines each local environment as one of four named Docker Compose stacks (auth, mcm, audit, observability), each its own Compose project whose aggregator file is an include:-only list of that stack's per-service compose files, and each brought up through an Nx target that pins the project name, the aggregator file and the stack's gitignored .env rather than a bare docker compose invocation.",
